# L §5.11 example def and version, copied whole (with the families, inputs and the source it names).
# Steps 2-6: before rm2016 governs (2016-03) the def's own base applies: max(0 PLN, 500.00 − 100.00) = 400.00 PLN,
# small's when (400.00 < 20.00) is false.  From 2016-04 the replacing version of base wins on its span (step 2):
# max(0 PLN, 600.00 − 100.00) = 500.00 PLN.  For f2 small applies (110.00 − 100.00 = 10.00 < 20.00) and beats
# base: 0 PLN, the money 0.00 PLN. (Writer 8: reasons() is gone, L §2.2; q2 read it.)
=== m.tally
model ul05
  tally 2
  on 2016-10-31
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source rm1238 "Rozporządzenie 2015"
source rm2016_act "Rozporządzenie 2016"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind families

input entitled[f in families, m in months]: money PLN
input entitled_2016[f in families, m in months]: money PLN
input excess[f in families, m in months]: money PLN
input min_payment: money PLN

def payable[f in families, m in months]: money PLN at start_of(m)
  note "kwota wypłacana po obniżeniu, art. 5 ust. 3"
  rule base = max(0 PLN, entitled[f, m] - excess[f, m])
  rule small beats base = 0 PLN when entitled[f, m] - excess[f, m] < min_payment

version rm2015
  cite rm1238
  governs 2015-11..
  known 2015-09-07
  families + [f1, f2] lives 2010-01-01..
  entitled[f1, *] = 500.00 PLN
  entitled[f2, *] = 110.00 PLN
  entitled_2016[f1, *] = 600.00 PLN
  entitled_2016[f2, *] = 110.00 PLN
  excess[*, *] = 100.00 PLN
  min_payment = 20.00 PLN

version rm2016
  cite rm2016_act
  governs 2016-04..
  known 2016-02-10
  replace rule payable.base = max(0 PLN, entitled_2016[f, m] - excess[f, m])

ask q1: payable[f1, 2016-03], payable[f1, 2016-05], payable[f2, 2016-05]
=== expect
q1: (400.00 PLN, 500.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
  cut 2016-10-31
